# {{project}}

Built with [fastapi-mvt](https://github.com/OdaiAhmed99/fastapi-mvt).

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[test]"
python manage.py makemigrations     # creates migrations/ and the first migration
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver          # http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
```

## Everyday commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `python manage.py startapp blog --crud Post` | New app with a model, schemas, CRUD router and tests |
| `python manage.py makemigrations` | Detect model changes and write a migration |
| `python manage.py migrate` | Apply migrations (`migrate 0003` moves back or forward) |
| `python manage.py showmigrations` | List migrations and whether they are applied |
| `python manage.py shell` | Python shell with your models loaded (top-level `await` works) |
| `python manage.py check` | Verify config, models and migrations (use it in CI) |
| `pytest` | Run tests against a throwaway test database |

## Layout

```
{{project}}/        settings, database, app wiring, auth
users/              the User model
tests/
migrations/         created by the first makemigrations
```
